[Music]  in tonight's special report focused on  the midterms bret bear interviews the  newest republican candidate for the  pennsylvania senate seat tv's dr oz  brett  thanks mike in tonight's special report  spotlight on the midterms the  pennsylvania senate race received some  star power this week dr mehmet oz of the  dr oz tv show is now running as a  republican candidate for senate the  current senator republican pat toomey  will not run for re-election one gop  candidate sean parnell who was endorsed  by former president trump has already  dropped out after a bitter custody  battle with his ex-wife  but there are still almost a dozen other  candidates in the republican side who  have announced and there are already a  dozen democrats in the running tonight  we have dr mehmet oz with us to explain  why he's entering the race dr oz thanks  for being here  glad to be with you brett so a lot of  people look at this and say why i mean  you've got a successful tv show you're  you've had a tremendous run  on television and around the world why  do this now  brett my parents were immigrants to this  country were afforded unbelievable  opportunities i owe a debt i've always  felt it  and america is in crisis now so i think  it's an ideal time for me to repay that  debt by serving this country and running  as a senator from the state of  pennsylvania i see our values under  attack many of the issues you talk about  frequently keep me up at night i believe  americans deserve better and there's  solutions out there that are evident  that we're not taken advantage of but we  are spending too much time  taking people who've got good ideas and  shaming them and silencing them and  bullying them and canceling them and  i'll tell you something in medicine if  we cannot say what we see with our own  eyes people die  and these choices i think should be the  people watching the show right now for  me specifically the people in  pennsylvania i have fought to empower  folks my whole career i've taken on big  pharma on the show i've taken on big  tech agrochemical companies i've got the  scars to prove it and i can't be bought  and this is the time if i'm ever going  to do it to jump out of the comfort and  the safety of a tv show or frankly even  in the operating room i don't get  attacked usually by people and starts  talking about things that really can  make our country succeed because i'm so  optimistic you know you have a primary  to go through on the republican side i  put up the candidates already out but  there's one that has not declared yet  but might david mccormick is being  recruited former treasury under  secretary for international affairs  combat veteran business executive  do you expect he's going to get in and  why are you better positioned if he does  i'm not sure what's going to happen with  mr mccormick i haven't spoken to him but  i know that i have 94 name recognition  in pennsylvania it's very hard to get  there takes years and years of hard work  and and lots of effort talking to people  in their own living rooms i know that i  fare well with republican audiences who  know that i share their values i don't  speak generally on the show of overtly  political issues but during covet i got  political because unfortunately if you  mix medicine politics you get politics  so i had to get engaged to try to help  our country deal with the fact that we  were myopically focused on some issues  and blind to others and we're taking  chances by using our children as shields  and addressing other changes that happen  to our society under the cover of covet  i want to talk to you about covet and  about the biden administration policy  but you mentioned pennsylvania  specifically and and you're running here  already there are some people that are  suggesting that you know you're moving  in basically to run for the senate seat  here is uh stephen colbert on this issue  he may have fake pennsylvania claims  because he's running there despite  living in new jersey for years and  there's a big difference between  pennsylvania and new jersey  something to do with hoagies i don't  know what it is but they will murder you  over it  now he's joking about the hoagies but  what about that the carpet bagging  charge  you know i grew up just south of here  i'm in philadelphia uh just across the  state border i went to medical school at  penn here in philadelphia i went to  wharton business school met my wife the  best decision of my life was marrying  her here in philadelphia at the church  just down the road from where i am now i  had my first two kids here i mean i  spent a lot of time in pennsylvania i  did move to new jersey because  television is done in new york city and  it was convenient but we came back here  all the time and we moved back last year  both to spend time with their parents  but also because this is home and we  feel very comfortable here you know you  mentioned covid and the policies  considering this travel restriction  based on this new omicron variant we've  had our first case discovered and there  probably have been cases here in the u.s  but the first official one in california  what what do you think about this biden  policy  yeah you know we we have  started off with very simple approaches  like we don't know what we're dealing  with let's let's bend the curve for two  weeks do you remember that comment brett  that metastasized into this overreaching  authoritarianism so now we almost had a  reflexive response and start doing  things we would never think of allowing  even two years ago and omicron is a  virus that has 50 mutations in it 32 on  the spike protein i've done my homework  on it we just don't know we don't know  if it's more contagious we don't know if  it's more likely to make you sick we  don't even know if it makes you more  likely to get ill if you've been  vaccinated so in the face of a lot of  unknowing we don't just go snap  decisions about big-time changes that  will affect our economy affect our  people and and bring fear to a  population is just getting out of the  original covent pandemic i think we need  to go slowly with a calm hand like you  would in surgery don't rush the  decisions and one thing i think we've  seen a lot of is people who just don't  know the answers start barking out  authoritarian comments because it makes  them seem like they're in control but if  you don't have a good understanding  what's going down it just means you're  making mistakes you know you run your  show you run your operating room when  you if you win are in the senate you're  one out of a hundred you okay with that  i'm okay you know in the operating room  you're not by yourself on this on the  show as you know where you are right now  there's a dozen people staring at you i  build teams i make sure we respect each  other we work together and that's why we  win because we work it together all  right 2004 oprah winfrey brings you on  the show uh you become a success and a  friend of hers obviously throughout she  is known to be a democrat  is she going to endorse this run  i actually spoke to oprah recently she  told me to follow my heart she's been a  wonderful mentor to me the fairest woman  i've ever worked with um and a great and  a sage advisor of mine i actually don't  want her to get involved in any way at  first i don't want to hurt her and the  biggest advice i'm getting from my  friends is thank you for doing this  because you're going to get hurt and i  think that's true so i don't want people  having to take bullets when i should be  taking them myself but i'll be calling  her and asking advice and uh and  interested in her comments uh but i  think both with oprah and many other  people in my life that have been mentors  of mine i want them safe  dr oz we'll be following this race  thanks for coming on  god bless you brett take care hey sean  hannity here hey click here to subscribe  to fox news youtube page and catch our  hottest interviews and most compelling  analysis you will not get it anywhere  else

